Verification: a real format-1 RocksDB checkpoint image is opened through `RocksDB.openReadOnly`. The physical inspector enforces finite file/byte bounds, exact column-family inventory, empty default column family with checked iterator status, manifest file length/checksum equality, and exact Store format/Shard/db identity/incarnation, checkpoint ID, applied source position, and mutation sequence. The state inventory scans every registered Column Family under finite record/byte/time bounds; it counts key-kind prefixes, decodes old Message status and retired identity records, and checks each Message key/source route belongs to the checkpoint Shard. For typed SCHEDULED records it rebuilds and verifies the due/ordered key from Message and source fields, then checks the persisted DUE/ORDERED and EXPIRY values. Missing indexes return a stable conflict bound to the old Message key digest and canonical source position. The manifest-bound physical inventory is checked before and after the logical scan. Tests cover valid indexes, a missing expiry-index conflict, malformed Message rejection without file changes, read-budget exhaustion, and a manifest/image mismatch.

Command:
`./gradlew test --tests 'com.nereusstream.delay.store.LegacyCheckpointImageInspectorTest' checkstyleTest`

`./gradlew checkDocumentation`

Result: 4 tests, 0 failures/errors/skips; `checkstyleTest` and `checkDocumentation` passed. `./gradlew checkstyleMain` reports only pre-existing 123-character lines in untouched `PersistentLaneScheduler.java:1327` and `TargetWorkerHostRuntime.java:347`.

Scope: this proves physical identity and a partial bounded relationship inventory for typed SCHEDULED timeline/expiry indexes only. It does not validate full legacy cross-record obligations, old TimelineEntry/Profile semantics, other owners and joins, replay source bytes after the checkpoint, produce the full per-Shard dry-run/disposition/conflict report, establish durable migration activation, convert a Store, or authorize rollback/reader retirement. B6 remains `IN_PROGRESS / PENDING_CENTRAL_VALIDATION`.
